The P1 DTU HPC is P1's partition at DTU. It suits medium to large-scale machine learning research
by P1 members (PhD and above).

## Getting Access

### Who's eligible?

**Requirements:** PhD or higher (exceptions may apply), valid Danish university email, and
registered P1 affiliation.

### Do I need to talk to someone first?

No. The optional [workload survey](p1:surveyPage) tells the P1 compute coordinator about your
workload, so we can point you to the right resource.

### How do I sign up?

1. Request P1 affiliation in [your P1 profile](p1:profile) (**Update Profile** in the header). P1
   staff approve it.
2. Fill in the DTU account form below. It only accepts official university email addresses.
   Henning Christiansen (head of DTU's compute centre) processes it, and you get the account
   details by email.

<EmbedForm
  title="DTU Account Signup Form"
  src="{DTU_SIGNUP_FORM_URL}?embed=true"
  href={DTU_SIGNUP_FORM_URL}
  description="Use your official university email address."
/>

### What if I don't qualify?

<AccessException />

## Connecting

The login node is `login9.hpc.dtu.dk`, and you can reach it from anywhere. Off DTU's network it
asks for your DTU password after your key. On DTU's network or the DTU VPN, the key is enough;
[DTU IT's VPN guide](https://www.hpc.dtu.dk/?page_id=2501) covers setup and MFA.

```bash
aicentre check -p dtu --connect
```

`aicentre check` shows the Host block for `~/.ssh/config` and whether your key is set up, then
tests the login.

## Using the Cluster

The cluster runs IBM Spectrum LSF with two queues:

- `p1`: batch jobs, seven nodes
- `p1i`: interactive sessions, one node, for installing packages, test runs and short debugging

`p1i` is the only P1 queue for interactive GPU work. Everything else runs as a batch job. Home
directories hold 30 GB, so project data goes under `/dtu/p1/`. See DTU's
[LSF guide](https://www.hpc.dtu.dk/?page_id=2698) for scheduler flags and its
[transfer nodes](https://www.hpc.dtu.dk/?page_id=2671) for very large data moves.

From the gallery:

- [an interactive session with a GPU](/gallery/int-gpu/) on `p1i`
- [VS Code on the login node](/gallery/rem-lgn/)
- [moving code and data](/gallery/xfr-dat/) on and off the cluster

See [every example that runs on P1 DTU HPC](/gallery/?provider=dtu).

## Policy & Support

### What are the limits?

<ClusterQuotas slug="dtu" />

For more storage, contact the governance group at
[compute-governance-p1@aicentre.dk](mailto:compute-governance-p1@aicentre.dk).

### How much storage do I get?

Your 500 GB project allowance comes out of a 60 TiB shared pool. Use it as working space, not an
archive. Keep code in git and a second copy of anything you cannot regenerate on institutional
storage or your own machine. Before a project ends, ask the compute coordinator what to move off.

<Aside type="caution" title="GDPR Compliance">

Only non-GDPR data belongs here, such as public datasets and open benchmarks. Your home directory
is private, but the cluster is not approved for personal data, whatever you do at file level. If
your project involves personal data, talk to the compute coordinator before you start.

</Aside>

